 # Hard Voxelization (Deterministic)
 
-Also called: Point Cloud Voxelization via Histogramming, Voxel Grid Downsampling, Voxelization of unstructured 3D data, voxel aggregation
+Also called: Voxelization (mmdet3d.ops.Voxelization), voxel_layer [S3, unofficial]
 
 ## Overview
-Hard Voxelization (Deterministic) converts an unstructured 3D point cloud into a fixed-size, regular voxel grid by partitioning space into cubic cells, aggregating point attributes within each cell, and outputting a single representative point (typically the centroid) per occupied voxel [S1, S2, S5, unofficial]. It solves the problem of downsampling dense, irregular point clouds into a structured format suitable for efficient neural network processing or volume rendering [S1, S2, unofficial]. Unlike its sibling [Fast Deterministic GPU Voxelization (Sort-Scatter)](3806-fast-deterministic-gpu-voxelization-sort-scatter.md), which uses parallel sorting for speed, this method relies on explicit coordinate quantization and unique-coordinate identification to guarantee bit-identical, reproducible output order regardless of hardware execution order [S3, unofficial]. It differs from [Grid Pooling (Max Pooling over Points)](4327-grid-pooling-max-pooling-over-points.md) by computing centroids (averages) rather than maximum values, and from [Voxel Hashing and Mean Aggregation](11234-voxel-hashing-and-mean-aggregation.md) by using a dense, pre-allocated grid structure rather than a sparse hash map [S1, S2, S3, unofficial].
+Hard Voxelization (Deterministic) converts an unstructured 3D point cloud into a fixed-size, regular voxel grid by partitioning space into cubic cells, aggregating point attributes within each cell, and outputting a single representative point (typically the centroid) per occupied voxel [S1, S2, S5, unofficial]. It solves the problem of downsampling dense, irregular point clouds into a structured format suitable for efficient neural network processing or volume rendering [S1, S2, unofficial]. Unlike its sibling [Fast Deterministic GPU Voxelization (Sort-Scatter)](3806-fast-deterministic-gpu-voxelization-sort-scatter.md), which uses parallel sorting for speed, this method relies on explicit coordinate quantization and unique-coordinate identification to guarantee bit-identical, reproducible output order regardless of hardware execution order [S3, unofficial]. It differs from [Grid Pooling (Max Pooling over Points)](4327-grid-pooling-max-pooling-over-points.md) by computing centroids (averages) rather than maximum values [S1, unofficial].
 
